# Tracked exclusions, root-anchored — the reviewable, clone-surviving
# rule (the per-clone .git/info/exclude carries legacy unanchored
# duplicates). /_handoff/ holds session material including raw
# external-audit texts that must never be committed (protected-name
# rule; ADR-0029 decision 6). Host-local instruction files (CLAUDE.md
# and any sibling) carry no normative authority (M3-PLAN §2 N1, R-min).
/_handoff/
/CLAUDE.md
# Editor-local residue: VS Code rewrites it on open, so deleting it is not
# durable and committing it would put one machine's editor state in the
# control repository. It failed the 2026-08-13 push door's porcelain check
# while being provably absent from everything pushed (operator ruling, that
# date). Root-anchored like the two rules above.
/.vscode/
# AGENTS.md at the root is the read-only-consultant instruction surface,
# installed under the M3 AGENTS-INSTALL approval and SHA-pinned in the
# operator's preflight baseline. Session material like CLAUDE.md above:
# never committed, no normative authority. Root-anchored like every rule
# in this file.
/AGENTS.md
